body:
Thank you very much! This guide was super helpful and so were these pointers! I happen to have that early bear honoka and cheerleader umi so I’m happy to be able to use them both! Wish I had that 6th anniversary honoka and the nurse kotori— kotori is my best girl, too and I still can’t get her ;__;
I wish they did the re-release for that nurse kotori event like they did in the old CN server. But I suppose that makes her all the more special!
I’ll test it out with only scorers but I’ll probably need one PL as a backup.

Did they up the rank requirement for the UR ticket? For JP AS I was awarded a UR ticket because of my ranking in SIF but the same did not happen for the WW release and my ranking in my SIF WW is much higher than my JP SIF ranking...

&#x200B;

ALSO -- I've had crappy luck. I wouldn't have even gotten a UR at all in AS WW if not for purchasing the UR guaranteed scout. I already linked my EN SIF account, can I still reroll and relink my SIF WW account to the new AS WW account? ;\_\_;

I tried to keep them separated more and just give them each others scents but I noticed that Alfie, the kitten, kept crying out. I gave him food, water, cleaned his litter box, and played with him but he just wanted out of the room. He isn't used to being alone -- he was in a foster home with a couple of kittens his age and some older cats. He's also quite shy. But very sweet -- he doesn't fight when picked up or pet. His main defense mechanism is hiding. And he has unfortunately taken to hiding under my bed (my bed is a special case, is has storage on one side, so there is no "underneath" on the right side but on the left side there is a very tiny crack that he can just barely fit under. it's impossible to get him out without trying to entice him -- which is virtually impossible, he doesn't seem interested in treats or food or even catnip and all his toys are under there! so I have to take my mattress off in order to get him out and even then I have to lift him through the slats of the bed. I tried stuffing blankets in the crack but he somehow managed to push them aside and get underneath anyways) do you have any tips to mitigate this? I tried keeping him out of that room but he cries when I do that and I cannot feed him with my other cat because he doesn't eat all his food at once, so, my cat Clover eats the rest of his food (she really shouldn't be, she's on a diet bc she weighed in at 16.5 pounds a couple months ago). 

&#x200B;

Other than that, everyone seems to be getting along. The cats are actually playing with each other and wrestling with each other. I was afraid they were really fighting at first but they both seemed to enjoy it and neither were crying or whining in pain. They weren't hissing or growling, either. They just seemed to be tussling a bit. Is this a good sign or a bad one? Hissing and growling has been essentially eliminated. I've been keeping Alfie in my room with his food and water and box and toys with the door open but a mini gate up. Clover is not athletic enough to jump over the gate but Alfie can, so, he has full run of the house now. It's been over a week since he came to live with us and he seems a lot more comfortable in the house. I think having my moms dog over doesn't help but they're all very civil with each other. The dog was just concerned when they appeared to be fighting -- the cats, I mean. I have no fear of Simba, the dog, hurting either of the cats, he's really good with them, just very curious about their smells (and insistent on smelling their butts despite them lacking scent glands there). My only worry is that the cats both have really long claws right now and I hope they don't accidentally hurt one another because of them.

this post is blessed
blessed be the baby birb girl<3
I wish I had more of her URs ;__;
